      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To determine how many minutes it will take for the printer to print 200 pages, we start by using the information given about the printer's printing rate and the total number of pages to be printed. The printer prints 17 pages per minute.\n\nWe can express the total time required to print 200 pages as the total number of pages divided by the printing rate:\n\\[\n\\text{Time} = \\frac{\\text{Total number of pages}}{\\text{Printing rate}} = \\frac{200 \\text{ pages}}{17 \\text{ pages per minute}}\n\\]\n\nNow, we perform the division:\n\\[\n\\text{Time} = \\frac{200}{17} \\approx 11.7647\n\\]\n\nSince we need to express the answer to the nearest whole number, we round 11.7647 to the nearest whole number. The closest whole number to 11.7647 is 12.\n\nTherefore, the time required to print 200 pages is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{12}\n\\]",
